<title>BELGIUM: BBL Switzerland says '96 profit up 15 pct.</title>
<headline>BBL Switzerland says '96 profit up 15 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banque Bruxelles Lambert (Suisee) SA, a unit of Belgium's bank BBL, said on Thursday 1996 consolidated net profit rose 15 percent to 19 million Swiss francs (about 450 million Belgian francs).</p>
<p>The unit, which specialises in private and institutional asset management as well as trade in commodities, said growth notably came from commission income, which rose 12 percent to 34 million Swiss francs.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
